    29.29,
    29.47,
    29.74,
    30.15,
    30.25,
    30.47
   ],
   "text": "In early 1933, a hundred-dollar bill was a claim on almost five ounces of gold. By the 1960s, less than three. Today, spend it on gold, and you'd get about a fortieth of an ounce."
  },
