    96.05
   ],
   "text": "More than twenty-five centuries ago, in Lydia, in what is now western Turkey, lumps of electrum, a natural mix of gold and silver, were stamped with a lion's head. They're among the earliest coins we know of. No more weighing metal at every sale. You could just count."
  },
