   "text": "America went further. On April 5th, 1933, in the depths of the Great Depression, President Franklin Roosevelt signed Executive Order 6102. Americans had to hand in most of their gold coins, bars and gold certificates by May 1st, paid at the official price of 20 dollars 67 cents an ounce."
  },
